{"chapter": "desirables", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02BM", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:34381e3e4fc24e2a78364e7d21d28d48e147e113380305c9f1072de783e826ec", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is perhaps one of the easier projects to work on, as most of the\nbasic theory is there now. Of course these things are really properties\nof morphisms of stacks. We can define singularities (up to smooth factors)\netc. Prove that a connected normal stack is irreducible, etc.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81ed041958cae86135d5caaaa2ea3a302231787a2c359189b858f65ab58bc6b4", "unit_id": "tag:02BM:paragraph-0001"}
